deep-research audit of the 019-skill-routing-refactor\n    parent packet surfaced 12 P1 + 5 P2 findings plus 3 policy questions. All fixed:\n    \n    Metadata/resume (P1.1-P1.3): dropped ghost 000-migration-plan from children_ids\n    (now 21, matches disk); regenerated description.json to the full 21-child scope;\n    set derived.last_active_child_id to the 020 router-unification program (live plan\n    of record). Fingerprints re-backfilled.\n    \n    Routing reference (P1.4-P1.6): resolved the 2-of-7 vs 7-of-7 rollout contradiction\n    (all 7 hubs ship surface routers/manifests, populated 7/7); corrected the default-mode\n    inventory (only sk-prompt named; sk-design/mcp-tooling/system-deep-loop/cli null-defer);\n    fixed the false sk-doc-only resourceContractVersion claim (all 7 registries declare 1).\n    \n    Before/after (P1.7-P1.8, P1.10): added the compiled-routing serving-authority note to\n    the After state; stated the real verification state (mutation teeth test complete\n    91/91 across 6 hubs, live-mode partial) instead of future tense; fixed smart_routing.md\n    to smart-routing.md (x2, current hyphenated canonical path).\n    \n    Links/topology (P1.9, sec.10): fixed the broken root Parent Spec pointer (top-level\n    packet, no parent); added a nested-topology note to context-index.md covering 020/007\n    duplicate-012 collision and the 14-child 015 sub-parent.\n    \n    Lifecycle authority (sec.9): documented the authority policy in context-index.md - child\n    graph-metadata.json is machine-authoritative for resume/traversal; parent narrative is\n    intent reconciled downward.\n    \n    P2: completed the handoff map for active D/E/F workstreams; corrected the only-authored-doc\n    note (context-index + 2 routing refs also exist); dropped 4 stale router-replay.cjs line\n    ranges (kept self-locating fn names); rooted 3 RELATED paths under .opencode/skills/;\n    disaggregated the conflated 7/7-hubs vs 91-of-106-scenarios metrics; 