{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784862681523,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_gBGvg1cvm35UfVYkEYlki0pE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n-None yet.\n+- Direct-child consistency: four PRE-EXISTING P1 defects verified in 012, 015, 017, and 019.\n+- Analogues beyond known defects: 015 and 019 have lifecycle/continuity contradictions; 013/014 and phase parents 020/021 were ruled out as false analogues.\n+- Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n-None yet.\n+- Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n@@\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n-None yet.\n+- Broad recursive validator output mixed nested descendants into direct-child evidence; use narrow direct-file verification for subsequent topology passes (iteration 1).\n@@\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n-None yet.\n+- Treating planned 013/014 implementation-summary absence as analogous to 012.\n+- Treating lean phase-parent 020/021 heavy-doc absence as a required-file defect.\n+- Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n@@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-All six key questions remain open.\n+- Nested lifecycle and resume topology remain unaudited.\n+- Parent routing references versus live runtime remain unaudited.\n+- Commit-level link/metric regression checks remain unaudited.\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Inventory and mechanically audit the 21 direct children for status, required-file, checklist, implementation-summary, and graph-metadata consistency.\n+Audit nested lifecycle topology and resume safety: parent and nested `children_ids`, `derived.last_active_child_id`, the 020/007 duplicate-012 prefix collision, and the 14-child 015 sub-parent.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@\n-{\"openQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"text\":\"Direct child packet consistency\"},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"text\":\"Analogous defects beyond 012 and 017\"},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"text\":\"Parent references versus live routing runtime\"},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"text\":\"New defects introduced by 140266be3e\"},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"text\":\"Lifecycle and nested topology truthfulness\"},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"text\":\"Cross-document link validity and resume safety\"}],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":6,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}\n+{\"openQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q3\",\"text\":\"Parent references versus live routing runtime\"},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"text\":\"Lifecycle and nested topology truthfulness\"},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"text\":\"Cross-document link validity and resume safety\"}],\"resolvedQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"text\":\"Direct child packet consistency\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"text\":\"Analogous defects beyond 012 and 017\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q4-direct-child-scope\",\"text\":\"New direct-child defects introduced by 140266be3e\",\"iteration\":1}],\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"012 fails required-file and level-consistency validation\"},{\"id\":\"f2\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"017 reproduces the memory-block validation defect\"},{\"id\":\"f3\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"015 spec and graph understate in-progress work as planned\"},{\"id\":\"f4\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"019 graph and continu