{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784862935516,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_vuXqKVujiSmGtpCij5oV04zR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Audit nested resume topology","subagent_type":"deep-research","command":"/deep:research:auto","prompt":"Execute exactly ONE deep-research iteration (iteration 2) for the initialized detached lineage. Read state first from `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/{deep-research-config.json,deep-research-state.jsonl,deep-research-strategy.md,findings-registry.json}`. Allowed writes ONLY under that lineage directory: `iterations/iteration-002.md`, one canonical state append, `deltas/iter-002.jsonl`, optional lineage-local `research.md`. Do not edit reducer-owned files. Focus exactly on lifecycle and resume safety across nested topology: verify parent `children_ids` and `derived.last_active_child_id`; inspect 020, 020/007, 020/007/015 and relevant nested graph metadata; test the duplicate `012-*` prefix collision under 020/007; inspect the claimed 14-child 015 sub-parent; identify whether basename/prefix selection can be ambiguous or stale. Exclude historical/frozen `research/**`, `benchmark/**`, `lineages/**`, `*.out`, `*.log`, and run-record artifacts as defect candidates. Every finding needs actual `file:line`, P1/P2, and NEW/PRE-EXISTING. Verify before report. Max-iterations policy: continue regardless of convergence telemetry. Mandatory route proof exactly as iteration 1. No sub-dispatch."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_06de4825afferz8MP95Fj0ETtw\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Iteration 2 Complete\n\n**Focus**: Nested lifecycle and resume safety across `019 → 020 → 007 → 015`  \n**Findings**: 4 new lineage findings; 3 P1 and 1 P2, all PRE-EXISTING  \n**newInfoRatio**: 1.0  \n**Questions answered**: Nested topology truthfulness; prefix and stale-pointer resume safety  \n**Questions remaining**: 2  \n