{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784862999187,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Hsq4JsUsiKOEWZZkYFUN1vl0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n@@\n - Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n+- Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n+- Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n@@\n - Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n+- Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n@@\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n@@\n - Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n+- Treating the 015 child-count claim as wrong; the count is 14, while its phase map exposes only 12.\n+- Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n@@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Nested lifecycle and resume topology remain unaudited.\n - Parent routing references versus live runtime remain unaudited.\n - Commit-level link/metric regression checks remain unaudited.\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit nested lifecycle topology and resume safety: parent and nested `children_ids`, `derived.last_active_child_id`, the 020/007 duplicate-012 prefix collision, and the 14-child 015 sub-parent.\n+Audit the four parent routing-reference documents against `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/` and all seven hubs' `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `leaf-manifest.json`, and `shared/references/smart-routing.md`.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@\n-{\"openQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q3\",\"text\":\"Parent references versus live routing runtime\"},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"text\":\"Lifecycle and nested topology truthfulness\"},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"text\":\"Cross-document link validity and resume safety\"}],\"resolvedQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"text\":\"Direct child packet consistency\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"text\":\"Analogous defects beyond 012 and 017\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q4-direct-child-scope\",\"text\":\"New direct-child defects introduced by 140266be3e\",\"iteration\":1}],\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"012 fails required-file and level-consistency validation\"},{\"id\":\"f2\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"017 reproduces the memory-block validation defect\"},{\"id\":\"f3\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"015 spec and graph understate in-progress work as planned\"},{\"id\":\"f4\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"019 graph and continuity metadata remain stale after research completion\"}],\"ruledOutDirections\":[\"013/014 as 012 analogues\",\"020/021 heavy-doc absence as defects\",\"140266be3e as source of direct-child defects\"],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":1,\"openQuestions\":3,\"resolvedQuestions\":3,\"keyFindings\":4,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{\"directChildren\":21}}}\n+{\"openQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q3\",\"text\":\"Parent references versus live routing runtime\"},{\"id\":\"q4-links\",\"text\":\"New link or metric defects introduced by 140266be3e\"}],\"resolvedQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"text\":\"Direct child packet consistency\",\"iteration\