{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784863512067,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_RuRL5BAAVI7X4lnP2nwAFdMr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n@@\n - Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n+- Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n@@\n - Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n+- Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n@@\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n@@\n - Broad recursive validator output mixed nested descendants into direct-child evidence; use narrow direct-file verification for subsequent topology passes (iteration 1).\n+- Exact 91/106 and 91/91 reproduction is unavailable from promoted non-frozen evidence; treat these as provenance gaps rather than false values (iteration 3).\n@@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Parent routing references versus live runtime remain unaudited.\n-- Commit-level link/metric regression checks remain unaudited.\n+- Full-tree cross-document link validity remains unaudited.\n+- Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n+- Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit the four parent routing-reference documents against `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/` and all seven hubs' `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `leaf-manifest.json`, and `shared/references/smart-routing.md`.\n+Audit all non-excluded Markdown and JSON cross-document links in the full packet tree; classify broken, stale, non-repo-rooted, and ambiguous links, with special attribution to `140266be3e`.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@\n-{\"openQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q3\",\"text\":\"Parent references versus live routing runtime\"},{\"id\":\"q4-links\",\"text\":\"New link or metric defects introduced by 140266be3e\"}],\"resolvedQuestions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"text\":\"Direct child packet consistency\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"text\":\"Analogous defects beyond 012 and 017\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q4-direct-child-scope\",\"text\":\"New direct-child defects introduced by 140266be3e\",\"iteration\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"text\":\"Lifecycle and nested topology truthfulness\",\"iteration\":2},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"text\":\"Nested resume safety\",\"iteration\":2}],\"keyFindings\":[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"012 fails required-file and level-consistency validation\"},{\"id\":\"f2\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"017 reproduces the memory-block validation defect\"},{\"id\":\"f3\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"015 spec and graph understate in-progress work as planned\"},{\"id\":\"f4\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"019 graph and continuity metadata remain stale after research completion\"},{\"id\":\"f5\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"Null pointers at 020 and 020/007 prevent deterministic automatic descent\"},{\"id\":\"f6\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"classification\":\"PRE-EXISTING\",\"summary\":\"Duplicate 012 phase numbers make numeric-only selection ambiguous\"},{\"id\":\"f7\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"classific