{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784863895446,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_FFpmTLtoA0bAjkqcfpZ7oDA6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n@@\n - Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n+- Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n@@\n - Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n+- Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n@@\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n@@\n - Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n+- Treating generic backticked filenames or logical `children_ids` as broken filesystem links without contextual/schema resolution.\n@@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Full-tree cross-document link validity remains unaudited.\n - Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n - Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit all non-excluded Markdown and JSON cross-document links in the full packet tree; classify broken, stale, non-repo-rooted, and ambiguous links, with special attribution to `140266be3e`.\n+Audit broad fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims against current promoted non-frozen evidence and executable checkers; identify overclaims and missing evidence boundaries.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -30,16 +30,18 @@\n - Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n - Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n - Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n - Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n+- Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n - Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n - Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n - Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n+- Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n@@ -58,20 +60,20 @@\n - Treating lean phase-parent 020/021 heavy-doc absence as a required-file defect.\n - Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n - Treating the 015 child-count claim as wrong; the count is 14, while its phase map exposes only 12.\n - Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n+- Treating generic backticked filenames or logical `children_ids` as broken filesystem links without contextual/schema resolution.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Full-tree cross-document link validity remains unaudited.\n - Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n - Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit all non-excluded Markdown and JSON cross-document links in the full packet tree; classify broken, stale, non-repo-rooted, and ambiguous links, with special attribution to `140266be3e`.\n+Audit broad fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims against current promoted non-frozen evidence and executable checkers; identify overclaims and missing evidence boundaries.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -30,16 +30,18 @@\n - Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n - Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n - Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n - Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n+- Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n - Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n - Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n - Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n+- Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n@@ -58,20 +60,20 @@\n - Treating lean phase-parent 020/021 heavy-doc absence as a required-file defect.\n - Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n - Treating the 015 child-count claim as wrong; the count is 14, while its phase map exposes only 12.\n - Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n+- Treating generic backticked filenames or logical `children_ids` as broken filesystem links without contextual/schema resolution.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Full-tree cross-document link validity remains unaudited.\n - Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n - Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit all non-excluded Markdown and JSON cross-document links in the full packet tree; classify broken, stale, non-repo-rooted, and ambiguous links, with special attribution to `140266be3e`.\n+Audit broad fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims against current promoted non-frozen evidence and executable checkers; identify overclaims and missing evidence boundaries.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n","additions":4,"deletions":2}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1784863895438,"end":1784863895445}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0434b327a165a9a6016a62dc8ed0f08191bebdb4b9c34622f6"}},"id":"prt_f922d8dfe001LO5IJrIa3FDFPU","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f922d5844001iAjDRKMMTMt3xg"}}
