{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784864227817,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_UAHyU5A9FmKMV9sYcOaQ756l","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n@@\n - Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n+- Fleet claims: 7/7 route-gold framing is NEW and wrong in denominator scope; nested 009 and 013 overclaim completion; fleet activation is real but hard-invariant closure is incomplete.\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n@@\n - Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n+- Pairing claim inventory with live route proof, checker execution, and checklist arithmetic separated serving activation from closure and lifecycle truth (iteration 5).\n@@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n - Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n+- Parent commit regression inventory should be closed with line-by-line changed-hunk review.\n+- Final deduplication and severity/classification reconciliation remain pending.\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit broad fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims against current promoted non-frozen evidence and executable checkers; identify overclaims and missing evidence boundaries.\n+Sample nested descendants outside the primary 019/020/007/015 path for status, checklist, summary, graph, and required-file consistency, prioritizing complete-status packets and unresolved P0/P1 gates.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -31,8 +31,9 @@\n - Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n - Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n - Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n - Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n+- Fleet claims: 7/7 route-gold framing is NEW and wrong in denominator scope; nested 009 and 013 overclaim completion; fleet activation is real but hard-invariant closure is incomplete.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n@@ -40,8 +41,9 @@\n - Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n - Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n - Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n - Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n+- Pairing claim inventory with live route proof, checker execution, and checklist arithmetic separated serving activation from closure and lifecycle truth (iteration 5).\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n@@ -65,15 +67,16 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Remaining fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims need promoted-evidence checks.\n - Nested descendants beyond the direct-child and 019/020/007/015 path need consistency sampling.\n+- Parent commit regression inventory should be closed with line-by-line changed-hunk review.\n+- Final deduplication and severity/classification reconciliation remain pending.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Audit broad fleet-wide PASS, authority, metric, and enforcement claims against current promoted non-frozen evidence and executable checkers; identify overclaims and missing evidence boundaries.\n+Sample nested descendants outside the primary 019/020/007/015 path for status, checklist, summary, graph, and required-file consistency, prioritizing complete-status packets and unresolved P0/P1 gates.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Devel