{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784865045933,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_hbPP64nqoBDcJGISYljQUibg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-007.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 7: Eight Out-of-Box Idea Child Packets\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: Audit all eight children under `020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives` for status truthfulness, declared documentation level and required files, implementation-summary/checklist/graph agreement, child and pointer semantics, and stale or broken canonical links. Frozen research, benchmark, lineage, log, output, and run-record artifacts were excluded. This follows the strategy's exact next focus and does not revisit unrelated branches.\n5: \n6: ## Findings\n7: 1. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — all eight children declare Level 2 but fail the same required-file contract.** Children 001-004 explicitly retain Level 2 and name `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `checklist.md` as canonical surfaces; children 005-008 explicitly score as Level 2 and prescribe those files, with 007-008 also naming `implementation-summary.md`. Exact filesystem probes found only `spec.md`, `presentation.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json` in every child; strict validation independently returned exit 2 and `FILE_EXISTS`, `LEVEL_MATCH`, and `SECTION_COUNTS` errors for all eight. Graph metadata reinforces the incomplete inventory by deriving only `spec.md` as a key/source document. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:146] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:68-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:67-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: exact on-disk target probes and eight strict validator runs show the declared canonical files are absent, not merely unindexed]\n8: 2. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — children 001-004 claim completion without checklist or implementation-summary evidence.** Each child spec says research is complete, and each graph says `complete`, but the required verification and current-state surfaces are absent, causing strict validation to skip both cross-document status and current-state checks. The graph's complete status is therefore not supported by the packet's own declared Level-2 evidence contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: actual target verification confirmed no checklist or implementation-summary exists in any of 001-004]\n9: 3. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the parent overstates children 005-007 as complete while their canonical graphs remain in progress.** The parent phase map says each completed a 5/5 dive plus presentation, but the three child graphs report `in_progress`; their specs say only “Research synthesized,” and their missing checklists/summaries prevent completion reconciliation. Child 008 is not part of this defect: its parent row, spec, and graph consistently say the dive has not run / remains in progress. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:43-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:33-35]\n10: 4. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the local phase-parent lifecycle is stale despite correct child identity semantics.** `children_ids` enumerates all eight exact canonical packet IDs, and each child correctly has no descendants, so there is no ID collision or child-list drift. However, the parent graph remains `planned` and leaves `last_active_child_id` null even though its own phase map says seven dives are complete and child 008 remains the active unfinished candidate. This prevents deterministic resume descent to 008 and misstates aggregate lifecycle. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:3-15] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:37-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:3-6] [INFERENCE: exact child-folder probes verified every listed target exists and that 008 is the sole map-declared unfinished child]\n11: \n12: All four findings are **PRE-EXISTING relative to commit `140266be3e`**: `git diff-tree --name-status 140266be3e -- <005 subtree>` returned no changed path, and parent-commit object probes confirmed each current `spec.md` and `graph-metadata.json` already existed while every missing canonical file was already absent. [INFERENCE: commit-tree and `140266be3e^` object verification against every audited child]\n13: \n14: ## Ruled Out\n15: - Broken or stale canonical links in this subtree: every explicit child and parent relative target resolved on disk, including all eight `presentation.md` files, source-lineage references, sibling phases 002/003/004/006/007, `GLM-cross-lineage-notes.md`, and parent specs.\n16: - `children_ids` drift or ambiguity: all eight exact IDs resolve to distinct existing folders, and every child correctly declares an empty child list.\n17: - Child 008 completion overclaim: its parent row, spec status, and graph status consistently preserve the not-yet-run state.\n18: - NEW defects from `140266be3e`: the commit touched no path in the audited subtree.\n19: \n20: ## Dead Ends\n21: None. The broad missing-file pattern is productive evidence, not an exhausted approach; future work should not re-run this exact eight-child inventory unless files change.\n22: \n23: ## Edge Cases\n24: - Ambiguous input: none; the exact eight-child subtree and excluded artifact classes were explicit.\n25: - Contradictory evidence: present — parent completion rows conflict with child graph/status evidence, and complete graphs lack completion surfaces.\n26: - Missing dependencies: none; the code graph was unavailable by known context, but direct canonical files, strict validation, target probes, and Git object checks were sufficient.\n27: - Partial success: none; all eight children, their local parent metadata, canonical links, and commit attribution were checked.\n28: \n29: ## Sources Consulted\n30: - `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-71`\n31: - `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:3-15,41-44,95-103`\n32: - Each child `spec.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json` under `001-*` through `008-*`\n33: - Eight strict `validate.sh <child> --strict` runs (all exit 2)\n34: - Exact filesystem target probes for required files, presentations, and relative links\n35: - `git diff-tree` and `git cat-file` checks against `140266be3e` and `140266be3e^`\n36: \n37: ## Assessment\n38: - New information ratio: 0.88\n39: - Questions addressed: eight-child lifecycle and required-file consistency; completion truthfulness; child/pointer semantics; canonical link validity; commit attribution\n40: - Questions answered: all eight children audited; every defect classified and attributed; no broken canonical link found\n41: \n42: ## Reflection\n43: - What worked and why: one bounded inventory, eight strict validators, exact relative-target resolution, and Git object probes separated shared structural defects from lifecycle contradictions and proved attribution without reading excluded evidence.\n44: - What did not work and why: metadata alone cannot validate completion because absent checklists and implementation summaries cause the validator to skip cross-document status checks.\n45: - What I would do differently: in the next branch audit, start with strict validation plus object-level attribution, then narrow reads only to contradictory files.\n46: \n47: ## Recommended Next Focus\n48: Perform the strategy's remaining line-by-line changed-hunk review of commit `140266be3e`, restricted to canonical non-frozen packet documents, then reconcile and deduplicate severities before iteration 10.\n\n(End of file - total 48 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 7: Eight Out-of-Box Idea Child Packets\n\n## Focus\nAudit all eight children under `020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives` for status truthfulness, declared documentation level and required files, implementation-summary/checklist/graph agreement, child and pointer semantics, and stale or broken canonical links. Frozen research, benchmark, lineage, log, output, and run-record artifacts were excluded. This follows the strategy's exact next focus and does not revisit unrelated branches.\n\n## Findings\n1. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — all eight children declare Level 2 but fail the same required-file contract.** Children 001-004 explicitly retain Level 2 and name `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `checklist.md` as canonical surfaces; children 005-008 explicitly score as Level 2 and prescribe those files, with 007-008 also naming `implementation-summary.md`. Exact filesystem probes found only `spec.md`, `presentation.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json` in every child; strict validation independently returned exit 2 and `FILE_EXISTS`, `LEVEL_MATCH`, and `SECTION_COUNTS` errors for all eight. Graph metadata reinforces the incomplete inventory by deriving only `spec.md` as a key/source document. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:146] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:68-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:67-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: exact on-disk target probes and eight strict validator runs show the declared canonical files are absent, not merely unindexed]\n2. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — children 001-004 claim completion without checklist or implementation-summary evidence.** Each child spec says research is complete, and each graph says `complete`, but the required verification and current-state surfaces are absent, causing strict validation to skip both cross-document status and current-state checks. The graph's complete status is therefore not supported by the packet's own declared Level-2 evidence contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: actual target verification confirmed no checklist or implementation-summary exists in any of 001-004]\n3. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the parent overstates children 005-007 as complete while their canonical graphs remain in progress.** The parent phase map says each completed a 5/5 dive plus presentation, but the three child graphs report `in_progress`; their specs say only “Research synthesized,” and their missing checklists/summaries prevent completion reconciliation. Child 008 is not part of this defect: its parent row, spec, and graph consistently say the dive has not run / remains in progress. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:43-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:33-35]\n4. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the local phase-parent lifecycle is stale despite correct child identity semantics.** `children_ids` enumerates all eight exact canonical packet IDs, and each child correctly has no descendants, so there is no ID collision or child-list drift. However, the parent graph remains `planned` and leaves `last_active_child_id` null even though its own phase map says seven dives are complete and child 008 remains the active unfinished candidate. This prevents deterministic resume descent to 008 and misstates aggregate lifecycle. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:3-15] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:37-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:3-6] [INFERENCE: exact child-folder probes verified every listed target exists and that 008 is the sole map-declared unfinished child]\n\nAll four findings are **PRE-EXISTING relative to commit `140266be3e`**: `git diff-tree --name-status 140266be3e -- <005 subtree>` returned no changed path, and parent-commit object probes confirmed each current `spec.md` and `graph-metadata.json` already existed while every missing canonical file was already absent. [INFERENCE: commit-tree and `140266be3e^` object verification against every audited child]\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Broken or stale canonical links in this subtree: every explicit child and parent relative target resolved on disk, including all eight `presentation.md` files, source-lineage references, sibling phases 002/003/004/006/007, `GLM-cross-lineage-notes.md`, and parent specs.\n- `children_ids` drift or ambiguity: all eight exact IDs resolve to distinct existing folders, and every child correctly declares an empty child list.\n- Child 008 completion overclaim: its parent row, spec status, and graph status consistently preserve the not-yet-run state.\n- NEW defects from `140266be3e`: the commit touched no path in the audited subtree.\n\n## Dead Ends","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-007.md","text":"# Iteration 7: Eight Out-of-Box Idea Child Packets\n\n## Focus\nAudit all eight children under `020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives` for status truthfulness, declared documentation level and required files, implementation-summary/checklist/graph agreement, child and pointer semantics, and stale or broken canonical links. Frozen research, benchmark, lineage, log, output, and run-record artifacts were excluded. This follows the strategy's exact next focus and does not revisit unrelated branches.\n\n## Findings\n1. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — all eight children declare Level 2 but fail the same required-file contract.** Children 001-004 explicitly retain Level 2 and name `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `checklist.md` as canonical surfaces; children 005-008 explicitly score as Level 2 and prescribe those files, with 007-008 also naming `implementation-summary.md`. Exact filesystem probes found only `spec.md`, `presentation.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json` in every child; strict validation independently returned exit 2 and `FILE_EXISTS`, `LEVEL_MATCH`, and `SECTION_COUNTS` errors for all eight. Graph metadata reinforces the incomplete inventory by deriving only `spec.md` as a key/source document. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:146] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:68-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:67-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: exact on-disk target probes and eight strict validator runs show the declared canonical files are absent, not merely unindexed]\n2. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — children 001-004 claim completion without checklist or implementation-summary evidence.** Each child spec says research is complete, and each graph says `complete`, but the required verification and current-state surfaces are absent, causing strict validation to skip both cross-document status and current-state checks. The graph's complete status is therefore not supported by the packet's own declared Level-2 evidence contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/002-replayable-correction-overlay/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/003-typed-no-destination/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [INFERENCE: actual target verification confirmed no checklist or implementation-summary exists in any of 001-004]\n3. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the parent overstates children 005-007 as complete while their canonical graphs remain in progress.** The parent phase map says each completed a 5/5 dive plus presentation, but the three child graphs report `in_progress`; their specs say only “Research synthesized,” and their missing checklists/summaries prevent completion reconciliation. Child 008 is not part of this defect: its parent row, spec, and graph consistently say the dive has not run / remains in progress. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:43-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/006-minimal-typed-contract/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:33-35]\n4. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING — the local phase-parent lifecycle is stale despite correct child identity semantics.** `children_ids` enumerates all eight exact canonical packet IDs, and each child correctly has no descendants, so there is no ID collision or child-list drift. However, the parent graph remains `planned` and leaves `last_active_child_id` null even though its own phase map says seven dives are complete and child 008 remains the active unfinished candidate. This prevents deterministic resume descent to 008 and misstates aggregate lifecycle. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:3-15] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:37-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/graph-metadata.json:3-6] [INFERENCE: exact child-folder probes verified every listed target exists and that 008 is the sole map-declared unfinished child]\n\nAll four findings are **PRE-EXISTING relative to commit `140266be3e`**: `git diff-tree --name-status 140266be3e -- <005 subtree>` returned no changed path, and parent-commit object probes confirmed each current `spec.md` and `graph-metadata.json` already existed while every missing canonical file was already absent. [INFERENCE: commit-tree and `140266be3e^` object verification against every audited child]\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Broken or stale canonical links in this subtree: every explicit child and parent relative target resolved on disk, including all eight `presentation.md` files, source-lineage references, sibling phases 002/003/004/006/007, `GLM-cross-lineage-notes.md`, and parent specs.\n- `children_ids` drift or ambiguity: all eight exact IDs resolve to distinct existing folders, and every child correctly declares an empty child list.\n- Child 008 completion overclaim: its parent row, spec status, and graph status consistently preserve the not-yet-run state.\n- NEW defects from `140266be3e`: the commit touched no path in the audited subtree.\n\n## Dead Ends\nNone. The broad missing-file pattern is productive evidence, not an exhausted approach; future work should not re-run this exact eight-child inventory unless files change.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Ambiguous input: none; the exact eight-child subtree and excluded artifact classes were explicit.\n- Contradictory evidence: present — parent completion rows conflict with child graph/status evidence, and complete graphs lack completion surfaces.\n- Missing dependencies: none; the code graph was unavailable by known context, but direct canonical files, strict validation, target probes, and Git object checks were sufficient.\n- Partial success: none; all eight children, their local parent metadata, canonical links, and commit attribution were checked.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n- `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-71`\n- `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:3-15,41-44,95-103`\n- Each child `spec.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json` under `001-*` through `008-*`\n- Eight strict `validate.sh <child> --strict` runs (all exit 2)\n- Exact filesystem target probes for required files, presentations, and relative links\n- `git diff-tree` and `git cat-file` checks against `140266be3e` and `140266be3e^`\n\n## Assessment\n- New information ratio: 0.88\n- Questions addressed: eight-child lifecycle and required-file consistency; completion truthfulness; child/pointer semantics; canonical link validity; commit attribution\n- Questions answered: all eight children audited; every defect classified and attributed; no broken canonical link found\n\n## Reflection\n- What worked and why: one bounded inventory, eight strict validators, exact relative-target resolution, and Git object probes separated shared structural defects from lifecycle contradictions and proved attribution without reading excluded evidence.\n- What did not work and why: metadata alone cannot validate completion because absent checklists and implementation summaries cause the validator to skip cross-document status checks.\n- What I would do differently: in the next branch audit, start with strict validation plus object-level attribution, then narrow reads only to contradictory files.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nPerform the strategy's remaining line-by-line changed-hunk review of commit `140266be3e`, restricted to canonical non-frozen packet documents, then reconcile and deduplicate severities before iteration 10.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":48,"totalLines":48,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-007.md","time":{"start":1784865045925,"end":1784865045931}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08f8ed04f8a21f9e016a62e115e12081918dad1c970badeaf8"}},"id":"prt_f923f3d95001YgBkUusfY4M0Oj","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f923ee2e5001vNKy7EYQ9g8WoZ"}}
