XISTING** — 020/005 children 001–004 claim complete without the checklist/summary evidence their Level-2 contract requires. | I7-F2 | Retained separately from CF-24 because unsupported completion is a distinct lifecycle claim. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/spec.md:25] |\n35: | CF-26 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — the 020/005 parent overstates children 005–007 as complete while their child graphs remain in progress. | I7-F3 | Retained and bounded to 005–007; child 008 is explicitly excluded. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:43-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/graph-metadata.json:33-35] |\n36: | CF-27 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — the 020/005 parent remains planned with a null active-child pointer although its phase map marks seven dives complete and identifies 008 as unfinished. | I7-F4 | Retained as a parent lifecycle/resume defect, separate from child completion claims. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103] |\n37: \n38: The canonical set therefore contains **27 active findings: 22 P1 and 5 P2; 4 NEW and 23 PRE-EXISTING**. [INFERENCE: arithmetic over CF-01 through CF-27]\n39: \n40: ## Duplicate Mappings\n41: - I5-F4 → CF-13 (exact reconfirmation of I3-F4).\n42: - I8's broken handoff-path duplicate → CF-14 (I4-F1).\n43: - I8's mixed 2/7-versus-7/7 duplicate → CF-09 (I3-F1).\n44: - I8's route-gold denominator duplicate → CF-18 (I5-F1).\n45: - I8's operator-gated/default-on duplicate → CF-11 and CF-12 (I3-F3 split by provenance).\n46: - I3-F5's metric claim was not retained as a defect; its only false portion is the 7/7 denominator already mapped to CF-18.\n47: - I6-F2 and the structural portion of I6-F3 → CF-22 (same Level-2 required-file contract across siblings).\n48: \n49: ## Ruled Out\n50: - **91/106 and 91/91 as false metrics:** ruled out. Current canonical evidence explicitly reports six applicable hubs, 106 total scenarios, 91 route-gold-applicable scenarios, and 91/91 mutation teeth. The defect is the parent’s “7/7 hubs PASS” denominator (CF-18); lack of raw frozen run records is a provenance limitation, not evidence that the arithmetic is false. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n51: - **Fleet compiled activation is false:** ruled out; CF-10 and CF-13 concern authority prose and broad invariant closure, not the existence of live compiled serving. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42]\n52: - **Canonical full-ID resume collides on duplicate `012`:** ruled out; only numeric/prefix-only selection is ambiguous (CF-06). [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535]\n53: - **015 has only 12 children:** ruled out; metadata lists 14, while the stale phase map exposes 12 (CF-07). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20]\n54: - All iteration-8 topology, root metadata/fingerprint, description truncation, default-mode, and activation candidates remain ruled out after deduplication. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:6-27] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/description.json:1-23]\n55: \n56: ## Dead Ends\n57: - Reopening frozen benchmark/run records cannot resolve a current defect under this lineage's scope. Canonical promoted evidence is sufficient to classify the metric arithmetic as supported-but-not-rawly-reproduced.\n58: - Re-running the complete direct-child or 020/005 inventories would duplicate exhausted approaches unless canonical files change.\n59: \n60: ## Edge Cases\n61: - Ambiguous input: none; “all findings” was interpreted as every finding in iterations 1–8, including duplicates and provenance limitations.\n62: - Contradictory evidence: metric scope, operator-gated/default-on prose, phase-parent status/pointers, and completion/checklist conflicts were reread from current canonical sources; unresolved claims were preserved as bounded contradictions.\n63: - Missing dependencies: raw frozen benchmark records remain excluded, but they are not required to distinguish a provenance limitation from CF-18's canonical denominator defect.\n64: - Partial success: none; every prior finding was mapped, retained, split, downgraded, merged, or ruled out.\n65: \n66: ## Sources Consulted\n67: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:145-161]\n68: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:40-58]\n69: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:40-68]\n70: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:124-134]\n71: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-46]\n72: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44]\n73: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103]\n74: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:45-48]\n75: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:105-106]\n76: \n77: ## Assessment\n78: - New information ratio: 0.10\n79: - Novelty justification: no external defect is new, but the +0.10 simplicity bonus applies because reconciliation reduced duplicate/ambiguous claims into one 27-finding model, split mixed provenance, and ruled a provenance limitation out as a defect.\n80: - Questions addressed: final finding deduplication; P1/P2 normalization; NEW/PRE-EXISTING normalization; false-claim versus provenance-limitation separation.\n81: - Questions answered: canonical finding set and duplicate map are complete for iterations 1–8.\n82: - Convergence telemetry only: iteration 10 remains mandatory under the max-iterations policy.\n83: \n84: ## Reflection\n85: - What worked and why: mapping every prior finding to a stable ID before changing severity exposed exact duplicates, mixed-provenance claims, and structural/lifecycle combinations that needed splitting.\n86: - What did not work and why: the reducer registry stopped at iteration 3, so it could not be treated as a complete finding inventory; iteration files and current canonical sources were required.\n87: - What I would do differently: maintain canonical IDs in each iteration delta from the first pass so final reconciliation becomes a mechanical fold rather than a prose crosswalk.\n88: \n89: ## Recommended Next Focus\n90: Iteration 10 should mechanically verify all 27 canonical source anchors, counts (22 P1/5 P2; 4 NEW/23 PRE-EXISTING), route fields, and packet-local artifacts, then perform terminal synthesis without reopening frozen evidence or adding duplicate findings.\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 9: Canonical Finding Reconciliation\n\n## Focus\nReconciled every finding from iterations 1–8 into one canonical set. Overlaps were merged, severity and `NEW`/`PRE-EXISTING` provenance were normalized, mixed-provenance claims were split, and overbroad claims were narrowed. Conflicts were decided from current canonical source files rather than prior summaries. Frozen artifacts remained excluded as defect candidates; lineage iterations were used only as reconciliation inputs. The fixed route was `mode=research target_agent=deep-research`; no sub-dispatch occurred.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Canonical finding | Source iterations | Decision and evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CF-01 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — direct child 012 declares Level 3 but lacks its required completion surface and fails the level/file contract. | I1-F1 | Retained and narrowed to the packet contract rather than treating every planned packet without a summary as defective. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:36-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/graph-metadata.json:43-49] |\n| CF-02 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — direct child 017 contains a structurally invalid `_memory.continuity` block despite otherwise consistent completion state. | I1-F2 | Retained; explicitly not a lifecycle disagreement. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/017-system-code-graph-routing-research/implementation-summary.md:10-39] |\n| CF-03 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — direct child 015 says Planned in spec/graph while its summary says In Progress and retains an open P1 gate. | I1-F3 | Retained. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/spec.md:58-65] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/implementation-summary.md:43-52] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/checklist.md:72-77] |\n| CF-04 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — direct child 019 claims research complete while graph and continuity remain in-progress/pending. | I1-F4 | Retained. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/spec.md:44-51] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/implementation-summary.md:13-27] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/graph-metadata.json:41-48] |\n| CF-05 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — null active-child pointers at 020 and 020/007 prevent deterministic automatic descent. | I2-F1 | Retained as one chain-level resume defect. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/graph-metadata.json:109-110] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/graph-metadata.json:111-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:504-535] |\n| CF-06 | **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** — duplicate `012-*` numbers are ambiguous only for numeric/prefix-only selection; complete canonical IDs remain unambiguous. | I2-F2 | Retained at P2 and narrowed so it does not imply a canonical-resume collision. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/spec.md:44-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535] |\n| CF-07 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — nested 015 metadata lists 14 children but its phase map exposes only 12, omitting 013 and 016. | I2-F3 | Retained; the child-count claim itself is true. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/spec.md:30-45] |\n| CF-08 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — nested 015 deterministically resumes to stale child 011 rather than later 013/016 work. | I2-F4 | Retained separately from the incomplete phase map because the pointer has an independent runtime effect. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:154-169] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/016-review-remediation/graph-metadata.json:196-217] |\n| CF-09 | **P1 · NEW** — the routing reference simultaneously says the typed resource surfaces are 2/7 and 7/7 populated. | I3-F1; I8 duplicate | Retained as an internal canonical contradiction introduced by `140266be3e`; current source still contains both claims. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:45-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:180-200] |\n| CF-10 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — parent prose conflates benchmark typed-resource replay with the live compiled destination-serving authority. | I3-F2 | Retained and narrowed: this does not dispute that compiled serving is live. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:64-68] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runti