CE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55] |\n| CF-19 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — nested 009 claims Complete while its P0 strict-validation gate remains failed/open. | I5-F2 | Retained at P1 because the unresolved gate is P0. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/009-sk-doc-template-alignment/checklist.md:103-139] |\n| CF-20 | **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** — nested 013 claims Complete/100% while P1/P2 items and operator sign-off remain open. | I5-F3 | **Downgraded P1→P2**: no unresolved P0 was cited and current compiled-serving truth remains supported; the defect is overbroad lifecycle closure. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:120-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:203-209] |\n| CF-21 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — 021 parent metadata remains planned with no active-child pointer although child 011 is active after completed predecessors. | I6-F1 | Retained as one parent lifecycle/resume defect. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/spec.md:10-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:45-48] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:105-106] |\n| CF-22 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — 020/004 and 020/006 both declare Level 2 but omit required canonical planning, checklist, and summary surfaces. | I6-F2 + I6-F3 structural portion | Merged the identical required-file defect across the two sibling packets. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:23-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/graph-metadata.json:32-36] |\n| CF-23 | **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** — 020/004 separately splits “Research complete” in spec from `in_progress` in graph. | I6-F3 lifecycle portion | **Split and downgraded from the original combined P1**: missing Level-2 files remain CF-22/P1; this status-only disagreement has no separately evidenced P1 runtime effect. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:10-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40] |\n| CF-24 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — all eight 020/005 idea children declare Level 2 but omit the required planning/verification surfaces. | I7-F1 | Retained as one bounded subtree-wide structural defect. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/spec.md:68-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72] |\n| CF-25 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — 020/005 children 001–004 claim complete without the checklist/summary evidence their Level-2 contract requires. | I7-F2 | Retained separately from CF-24 because unsupported completion is a distinct lifecycle claim. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/004-no-wrong-door-handoff/spec.md:25] |\n| CF-26 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — the 020/005 parent overstates children 005–007 as complete while their child graphs remain in progress. | I7-F3 | Retained and bounded to 005–007; child 008 is explicitly excluded. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:43-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/005-calibrated-negotiation/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/007-proof-carrying-commit/graph-metadata.json:33-35] |\n| CF-27 | **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** — the 020/005 parent remains planned with a null active-child pointer although its phase map marks seven dives complete and identifies 008 as unfinished. | I7-F4 | Retained as a parent lifecycle/resume defect, separate from child completion claims. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103] |\n\nThe canonical set therefore contains **27 active findings: 22 P1 and 5 P2; 4 NEW and 23 PRE-EXISTING**. [INFERENCE: arithmetic over CF-01 through CF-27]\n\n## Duplicate Mappings\n- I5-F4 → CF-13 (exact reconfirmation of I3-F4).\n- I8's broken handoff-path duplicate → CF-14 (I4-F1).\n- I8's mixed 2/7-versus-7/7 duplicate → CF-09 (I3-F1).\n- I8's route-gold denominator duplicate → CF-18 (I5-F1).\n- I8's operator-gated/default-on duplicate → CF-11 and CF-12 (I3-F3 split by provenance).\n- I3-F5's metric claim was not retained as a defect; its only false portion is the 7/7 denominator already mapped to CF-18.\n- I6-F2 and the structural portion of I6-F3 → CF-22 (same Level-2 required-file contract across siblings).\n\n## Ruled Out\n- **91/106 and 91/91 as false metrics:** ruled out. Current canonical evidence explicitly reports six applicable hubs, 106 total scenarios, 91 route-gold-applicable scenarios, and 91/91 mutation teeth. The defect is the parent’s “7/7 hubs PASS” denominator (CF-18); lack of raw frozen run records is a provenance limitation, not evidence that the arithmetic is false. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n- **Fleet compiled activation is false:** ruled out; CF-10 and CF-13 concern authority prose and broad invariant closure, not the existence of live compiled serving. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42]\n- **Canonical full-ID resume collides on duplicate `012`:** ruled out; only numeric/prefix-only selection is ambiguous (CF-06). [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535]\n- **015 has only 12 children:** ruled out; metadata lists 14, while the stale phase map exposes 12 (CF-07). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20]\n- All iteration-8 topology, root metadata/fingerprint, description truncation, default-mode, and activation candidates remain ruled out after deduplication. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:6-27] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/description.json:1-23]\n\n## Dead Ends\n- Reopening frozen benchmark/run records cannot resolve a current defect under this lineage's scope. Canonical promoted evidence is sufficient to classify the metric arithmetic as supported-but-not-rawly-reproduced.\n- Re-running the complete direct-child or 020/005 inventories would duplicate exhausted approaches unless canonical files change.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Ambiguous input: none; “all findings” was interpreted as every finding in iterations 1–8, including duplicates and provenance limitations.\n- Contradictory evidence: metric scope, operator-gated/default-on prose, phase-parent status/pointers, and completion/checklist conflicts were reread from current canonical sources; unresolved claims were preserved as bounded contradictions.\n- Missing dependencies: raw frozen benchmark records remain excluded, but they are not required to distinguish a provenance limitation from CF-18's canonical denominator defect.\n- Partial success: none; every prior finding was mapped, retained, split, downgraded, merged, or ruled out.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:145-161]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:40-58]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:40-68]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:124-134]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:35-46]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:45-48]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:105-106]\n\n## Assessment\n- New information ratio: 0.10\n- Novelty justification: no external defect is new, but the +0.10 simplicity bonus applies because reconciliation reduced duplicate/ambiguous claims into one 27-finding model, split mixed provenance, and ruled a provenance limitation out as a defect.\n- Questions addressed: final finding deduplication; P1/P2 normalization; NEW/PRE-EXISTING normalization; false-claim versus provenance-limitation separation.\n- Questions answered: canonical finding set and duplicate map are complete for iterations 1–8.\n- Convergence telemetry only: iteration 10 remains mandatory under the max-iterations policy.\n\n## Reflection\n- What worked and why: mapping every prior finding to a stable ID before changing severity exposed exact duplicates, mixed-provenance claims, and structural/lifecycle combinations that needed splitting.\n- What did not work and why: the reducer registry stopped at iteration 3, so it could not be treated as a complete finding inventory; iteration files and current canonical sources were required.\n- What I would do differently: maintain canonical IDs in each iteration delta from the first pass so final reconciliation becomes a mechanical fold rather than a prose crosswalk.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nIteration 10 should mechanically verify all 27 canonical source anchors, counts (22 P1/5 P2; 4 NEW/23 PRE-EXISTING), route fields, and packet-local artifacts, then perform terminal synthesis without reopening frozen evidence or adding duplicate findings.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":90,"totalLines":90,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md","time":{"start":1784865898843,"end":1784865898849}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0c9277525004b7a0016a62e46ac748819182c656afdcd75f31"}},"id":"prt_f924c4141001CbetO9vsLX2WoK","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f924c2513001sLFVnqLVfLXdQU"}}
