ified the iteration-9 canonical finding set, lineage-local artifact sequence, canonical state/delta records, packet boundary, route-proof fields, exclusion discipline, and terminal stop condition. This was the mandatory tenth and final iteration before synthesis. The exact route for this iteration is `mode=research target_agent=deep-research`; no sub-dispatch occurred.\n\n## Findings\n1. All 27 canonical findings retain resolvable real source anchors: 62 of 62 cited `file:line` or `file:line-range` anchors exist, are within the current file bounds, and contain non-empty source text. No source correction is required, so no duplicate defect finding is added. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md:8-38] [INFERENCE: mechanical resolution of every SOURCE marker in CF-01 through CF-27 against the current workspace]\n2. The canonical arithmetic remains exact: 27 findings comprise 22 P1 and 5 P2, with 4 NEW and 23 PRE-EXISTING. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md:10-38] [INFERENCE: classification count over the 27 canonical table rows]\n3. Before this write, iterations 001-009 and deltas 001-009 existed inside the lineage packet, each delta's first JSON object equaled its corresponding canonical state record, and iteration/delta 010 were absent. After this write, the intended sequence is exactly 001-010 for both classes and the state has exactly ten iteration records. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:1-11] [INFERENCE: packet-local artifact matrix and parsed JSON equality checks]\n4. Every prior iteration record has the base route-proof fields `mode=research`, `target_agent=deep-research`, and `agent_definition_loaded=true`. The exact canonical `resolved_route` is present in iterations 1-5, 7, and 9; iterations 6 and 8 honestly deviate by appending `route_proof=deep-research-skill-loaded; no_subdispatch=true`. Iterations 1-5 do not carry the later `routeProof` object; iteration 6 records no-subdispatch only in its suffixed route string; iterations 7-9 carry the object. Prior append-only records were not rewritten. Iteration 10 records the exact canonical `resolved_route`, an explicit exact `route`, and complete `routeProof`. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:2-11]\n5. No CF-01 through CF-27 source anchor points into excluded `research/**`, `benchmark/**`, `lineages/**`, `*.out`, or `*.log` artifact classes; those classes were not promoted as defects. The lineage iteration sources used here are mechanical verification evidence only, not canonical defect evidence. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:16-20] [INFERENCE: excluded-class scan over all 62 canonical source paths]\n6. The configured ceiling is exactly `maxIterations=10` with `stopPolicy=max-iterations`; this tenth record therefore terminates the loop with `stopReason=maxIterationsReached`. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:3-16] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:22-24]\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Source-anchor correction: ruled out because all 62 canonical anchors resolved to current non-empty file ranges.\n- Count correction: ruled out because both severity and provenance totals reproduce exactly.\n- Rewriting iterations 6 or 8 to normalize `resolved_route`: ruled out because prior state is append-only; their suffix deviations are preserved and disclosed.\n- Promoting frozen or excluded artifact classes as defects: ruled out by the canonical-source scan and the strategy boundary.\n\n## Dead Ends\n- Reopening excluded benchmark, lineage, output, log, or run-record artifacts would violate the frozen evidence boundary and is unnecessary for terminal verification.\n- Re-running exhausted direct-child or 020/005 inventories would add duplicate evidence rather than test the terminal mechanics.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Ambiguous input: none; “route string deviations” was interpreted literally against `Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research`.\n- Contradictory evidence: none in the canonical source verification. Route formatting is heterogeneous but transparently recorded rather than contradictory about the selected mode or agent.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none; all requested mechanical checks completed.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:1-40]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:1-11]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:1-99]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md:1-90]\n- The 62 current canonical source anchors listed in CF-01 through CF-27.\n\n## Assessment\n- New information ratio: 0.10\n- Novelty justification: no new defect was found; the +0.10 simplicity bonus reflects terminal closure of anchor validity, artifact integrity, route deviations, exclusion discipline, and stop semantics.\n- Questions addressed: canonical source validity; severity/provenance arithmetic; 001-010 artifact integrity; canonical state/delta equivalence; packet scope; route proof; excluded classes; terminal stop.\n- Questions answered: all terminal mechanical verification questions.\n\n## Reflection\n- What worked and why: parsing the canonical table and resolving every source marker mechanically avoided selective rereads and made the 62/62 result reproducible.\n- What did not work and why: prior route metadata is not uniform; iterations 6 and 8 suffix `resolved_route`, and early records lack the later structured `routeProof` object.\n- What I would do differently: require the exact `resolved_route`, explicit `route`, and structured `routeProof` schema from iteration 1 so terminal verification does not need to classify harmless formatting drift.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nProceed to reducer-owned terminal synthesis. Do not run iteration 11: `maxIterations=10` has been reached and the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":49,"totalLines":49,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-010.md","time":{"start":1784866164639,"end":1784866164645}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0c940982c83315fd016a62e5748e608191814046f74932d755"}},"id":"prt_f92504f71001RPLJD2DDnlzQl8","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f9250114b001CxPiUQfjwEPhw5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784866164742,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PVYV8dxEZC8npNrQfJelvGdx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Progressive Research Synthesis\n2: \n3: ## Iteration 1 — Direct-Child Packet Consistency\n4: \n5: The 21 immediate child packets were inventoried at direct depth. Four **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** defects were verified: 012 fails strict required-file and level-consistency checks; 017 reproduces three strict `_memory` block errors; 015 says Planned in spec/graph while its summary says In Progress (~70%); and 019 says Research Complete in spec/summary while graph and continuity metadata remain stale. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:36-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/017-system-code-graph-routing-research/implementation-summary.md:10-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/spec.md:58-65] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/implementation-summary.md:43-52] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/spec.md:44-51] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/graph-metadata.json:41-48]\n6: \n7: 013 and 014 pass strict required-file/level checks in their planned state, and 020/021 are lean phase parents; these were ruled out as analogous direct-child required-file defects. No canonical direct-child packet file was changed by commit `140266be3e`, so this iteration found no NEW direct-child defect. [INFERENCE: based on direct-child strict validation and `git show --name-only 140266be3e`]\n8: \n9: ## Iteration 2 — Nested Lifecycle and Resume Safety\n10: \n11: The root resume pointer correctly selects `020`, but `020` and `020/007` both leave `derived.last_active_child_id` null, so deterministic descent stops before the active nested work. The `015` sub-parent has a different failure: its pointer deterministically selects `011`, but that pointer predates later `013` and `016` work and is stale. All are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:122-123] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/graph-metadata.json:109-110] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/graph-metadata.json:111-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:154-169]\n12: \n13: The `015` child count is genuinely 14, but its canonical map lists only 12 rows and omits later children `013` and `016` (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). The duplicate `012-*` folders are a **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** numeric-selection risk, not a collision for canonical resume: the resolver tests complete normalized IDs/paths and complete basenames rather than three-digit prefixes. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/spec.md:30-45] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/spec.md:44-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535]\n14: \n15: ## Iteration 3 — Parent Canon versus Live Seven-Hub Runtime\n16: \n17: All seven live hubs carry `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `leaf-manifest.json`, and hub-level `shared/references/smart-routing.md`; every registry and manifest declares `resourceContractVersion: 1`, mode counts match, and only sk-prompt has a named default. The canonical reference nevertheless contains simultaneous 2/7 and 7/7 rollout claims (**P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:45-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:122-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:180-200] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/serving-closure.manifest.json:5-13]\n18: \n19: The promoted runtime is already default-on and compiled-authoritative for all seven hubs; `context-index.md`'s operator-gated-default claim is **P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**, while `spec.md`'s equivalent is **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. The reference also conflates benchmark surface-resource replay with the live compiled destination-serving path (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:108-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:71-75] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs:94-107]\n20: \n21: Canonical enforcement passed manifest guards 10a-10d on all seven hubs, but sk-design still fails hard topology invariant 6a because `styles/` is unregistered/unallowlisted (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). Exact 91/106 and 91/91 policy metrics added by `140266be3e` remain unsupported by promoted non-frozen runtime evidence under this iteration's exclusion boundary (**P2 · NEW**, provenance limitation rather than disproven values). [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs:895-899] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/mode-registry.json:39-165] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161]\n22: \n23: ## Iteration 4 — Full-Tree Cross-Document Links\n24: \n25: The parent handoff table added by `140266be3e` names nonexistent `020/spec.md` and `021/spec.md` targets instead of the full nested-parent folder names (**P1 · NEW**). Canonical child docs also retain pre-migration repo paths: 012 uses stale snake_case sk-doc names, and 013 uses the removed `mcp_server` and `skill_advisor_hook.md` names (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:133] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:112-125] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/013-skill-advisor-routing-fixes/tasks.md:67-74]\n26: \n27: The nested 020 migration map's “New location” values duplicate `020-router-unification-program/` when interpreted relative to their own document and work only under an unstated packet-root base (**P2 · PRE-EXISTING**). Historical rename links were excluded, and no broken Markdown link-syntax target survived exact resolution. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/context-index.md:13-22]\n28: \n29: ## Iteration 5 — Fleet Claims, Enforcement, and Lifecycle Completion\n30: \n31: The parent’s new “7/7 hubs PASS” route-gold framing is broader than its canonical evidence: `sk-design` is counted as PASS with 0/0 applicable cases, while the verification report defines six applicable hubs. The false claim is the 7/7 coverage framing; 91/106 and 91/91 remain provenance-limited rather than disproven because raw run records are excluded. **P1 · NEW.** [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/implementation-summary.md:58-66] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n32: \n33: Two nested lifecycle packets overclaim completion. `009-sk-doc-template-alignment` says Complete while its P0 strict-validation gate fails and only 12/13 P0 items are verified; `013-compiled-coverage-buildout` says Complete/100% while reporting 13/17 P1, 4/5 P2, and no formal operator sign-off. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/009-sk-doc-template-alignment/checklist.md:103-139] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:120-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:203-209]\n34: \n35: Mandatory route proof confirmed generation/hash-bound compiled decisions for all seven hubs, but `parent-skill-check.cjs` still fails sk-design invariant 6a on unregistered `styles/`. Fleet activation is live; complete parent-hub invariant closure is not. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**, reconfirmed. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs:884-900] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/README.md:1]\n36: \n37: ## Iteration 6 — Nested Descendants Outside 020/007/015\n38: \n39: The 021 parent lifecycle graph is stale: it remains planned and has no active-child pointer although phases 001-010 shipped and child 011 remains in progress. This is **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** and prevents deterministic descent to the active remediation packet. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/spec.md:10-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:45-48] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:105-106]\n40: \n41: Two additional Level-2 descendants under 020 are structurally incomplete. `006-unified-refactor-research` claims complete/strict-clean but lacks plan, tasks, checklist, and implementation summary; `004-oob-glm-parallel-research` lacks the same files and also splits “Research complete” in spec from `in_progress` in graph. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**; `140266be3e` changed neither subtree. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:11-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:23-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:10-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40]\n42: \n43: ## Iteration 7 — Eight Out-of-Box Idea Children\n44: \n45: All eight `020/005` idea children declare Level 2 but lack the required planning and verification files; all eight strict validators exit 2. Children 001-004 additionally claim complete in spec and graph without checklist or implementation-summary evidence. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** patterns. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72]\n46: \n47: The phase map overstates children 005-007 as complete while their child graphs remain in progress, and the local parent graph remains planned with a null active-child pointer despite seven completed rows and unfinished child 008. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. The exact eight `children_ids` and all explicit canonical links resolve correctly; 008 truthfully remains unfinished. Commit `140266be3e` touched no path in this subtree, and object probes confirm all defects predate it. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:37-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:6-15] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103]\n48: \n49: ## Iteration 9 — Canonical Finding Reconciliation\n50: \n51: Iterations 1–8 reconcile to **27 active findings: 22 P1 and 5 P2; 4 NEW and 23 PRE-EXISTING**. Exact duplicates were collapsed, the operator-gated/default-on claim was split into NEW `context-index.md` and PRE-EXISTING `spec.md` findings, and the combined 020/004 defect was split into a P1 required-file defect shared with 020/006 plus a P2 lifecycle-status disagreement. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:108-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:71-75] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:10-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:23-31]\n52: \n53: Three severity changes were made explicit: broken parent handoff paths were downgraded P1→P2 because they are recoverable navigation references; nested 013 completion overclaim was downgraded P1→P2 because no P0 remains open and serving truth is supported; and 020/004's status-only portion was split/downgraded to P2 while its structural file-contract failure remains P1. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:124-134] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:120-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40]\n54: \n55: The 91/106 and 91/91 figures are no longer a defect finding. Current canonical evidence supports that arithmetic over six applicable hubs; only the parent’s “7/7 hubs PASS” denominator remains **P1 · NEW**. Excluded raw run records limit provenance/reproduction but do not make the canonical figures false. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n56: \n57: ## Iteration 10 — Terminal Mechanical Verification\n58: \n59: All 27 canonical findings passed terminal source verification: 62/62 `file:line` anchors resolve to current non-empty ranges, and the totals remain **22 P1/5 P2** and **4 NEW/23 PRE-EXISTING**. No correction or duplicate defect finding was added. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md:8-38]\n60: \n61: The lineage now contains exactly iterations 001-010, deltas 001-010, and ten canonical state records inside the configured packet boundary. Earlier route strings were preserved append-only: iterations 6 and 8 append route-proof text to `resolved_route`, while iteration 10 carries the exact canonical `resolved_route`, explicit `route`, and structured no-subdispatch proof. No excluded artifact class was promoted as a defect. The configured tenth-iteration ceiling is reached with stop reason `maxIterationsReached`. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:3-18] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:2-11]\n\n(End of file - total 61 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Progressive Research Synthesis\n\n## Iteration 1 — Direct-Child Packet Consistency\n\nThe 21 immediate child packets were inventoried at direct depth. Four **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** defects were verified: 012 fails strict required-file and level-consistency checks; 017 reproduces three strict `_memory` block errors; 015 says Planned in spec/graph while its summary says In Progress (~70%); and 019 says Research Complete in spec/summary while graph and continuity metadata remain stale. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:36-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/017-system-code-graph-routing-research/implementation-summary.md:10-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/spec.md:58-65] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/implementation-summary.md:43-52] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/spec.md:44-51] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/graph-metadata.json:41-48]\n\n013 and 014 pass strict required-file/level checks in their planned state, and 020/021 are lean phase parents; these were ruled out as analogous direct-child required-file defects. No canonical direct-child packet file was changed by commit `140266be3e`, so this iteration found no NEW direct-child defect. [INFERENCE: based on direct-child strict validation and `git show --name-only 140266be3e`]\n\n## Iteration 2 — Nested Lifecycle and Resume Safety\n\nThe root resume pointer correctly selects `020`, but `020` and `020/007` both leave `derived.last_active_child_id` null, so deterministic descent stops before the active nested work. The `015` sub-parent has a different failure: its pointer deterministically selects `011`, but that pointer predates later `013` and `016` work and is stale. All are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:122-123] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/graph-metadata.json:109-110] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/graph-metadata.json:111-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:154-169]\n\nThe `015` child count is genuinely 14, but its canonical map lists only 12 rows and omits later children `013` and `016` (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). The duplicate `012-*` folders are a **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** numeric-selection risk, not a collision for canonical resume: the resolver tests complete normalized IDs/paths and complete basenames rather than three-digit prefixes. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/spec.md:30-45] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/spec.md:44-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535]\n\n## Iteration 3 — Parent Canon versus Live Seven-Hub Runtime\n\nAll seven live hubs carry `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `leaf-manifest.json`, and hub-level `shared/references/smart-routing.md`; every registry and manifest declares `resourceContractVersion: 1`, mode counts match, and only sk-prompt has a named default. The canonical reference nevertheless contains simultaneous 2/7 and 7/7 rollout claims (**P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:45-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:122-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:180-200] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/serving-closure.manifest.json:5-13]\n\nThe promoted runtime is already default-on and compiled-authoritative for all seven hubs; `context-index.md`'s operator-gated-default claim is **P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**, while `spec.md`'s equivalent is **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. The reference also conflates benchmark surface-resource replay with the live compiled destination-serving path (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:108-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:71-75] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs:94-107]\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/research.md","text":"# Progressive Research Synthesis\n\n## Iteration 1 — Direct-Child Packet Consistency\n\nThe 21 immediate child packets were inventoried at direct depth. Four **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** defects were verified: 012 fails strict required-file and level-consistency checks; 017 reproduces three strict `_memory` block errors; 015 says Planned in spec/graph while its summary says In Progress (~70%); and 019 says Research Complete in spec/summary while graph and continuity metadata remain stale. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:36-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/017-system-code-graph-routing-research/implementation-summary.md:10-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/spec.md:58-65] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-sk-code-router-alignment/implementation-summary.md:43-52] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/spec.md:44-51] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/019-sk-prompt-routing-research/graph-metadata.json:41-48]\n\n013 and 014 pass strict required-file/level checks in their planned state, and 020/021 are lean phase parents; these were ruled out as analogous direct-child required-file defects. No canonical direct-child packet file was changed by commit `140266be3e`, so this iteration found no NEW direct-child defect. [INFERENCE: based on direct-child strict validation and `git show --name-only 140266be3e`]\n\n## Iteration 2 — Nested Lifecycle and Resume Safety\n\nThe root resume pointer correctly selects `020`, but `020` and `020/007` both leave `derived.last_active_child_id` null, so deterministic descent stops before the active nested work. The `015` sub-parent has a different failure: its pointer deterministically selects `011`, but that pointer predates later `013` and `016` work and is stale. All are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:122-123] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/graph-metadata.json:109-110] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/graph-metadata.json:111-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:154-169]\n\nThe `015` child count is genuinely 14, but its canonical map lists only 12 rows and omits later children `013` and `016` (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). The duplicate `012-*` folders are a **P2 · PRE-EXISTING** numeric-selection risk, not a collision for canonical resume: the resolver tests complete normalized IDs/paths and complete basenames rather than three-digit prefixes. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/graph-metadata.json:6-20] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/spec.md:30-45] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/spec.md:44-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts:519-535]\n\n## Iteration 3 — Parent Canon versus Live Seven-Hub Runtime\n\nAll seven live hubs carry `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `leaf-manifest.json`, and hub-level `shared/references/smart-routing.md`; every registry and manifest declares `resourceContractVersion: 1`, mode counts match, and only sk-prompt has a named default. The canonical reference nevertheless contains simultaneous 2/7 and 7/7 rollout claims (**P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:45-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:122-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:180-200] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/serving-closure.manifest.json:5-13]\n\nThe promoted runtime is already default-on and compiled-authoritative for all seven hubs; `context-index.md`'s operator-gated-default claim is **P1 · NEW from `140266be3e`**, while `spec.md`'s equivalent is **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. The reference also conflates benchmark surface-resource replay with the live compiled destination-serving path (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:108-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:71-75] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs:94-107]\n\nCanonical enforcement passed manifest guards 10a-10d on all seven hubs, but sk-design still fails hard topology invariant 6a because `styles/` is unregistered/unallowlisted (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). Exact 91/106 and 91/91 policy metrics added by `140266be3e` remain unsupported by promoted non-frozen runtime evidence under this iteration's exclusion boundary (**P2 · NEW**, provenance limitation rather than disproven values). [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs:895-899] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/mode-registry.json:39-165] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161]\n\n## Iteration 4 — Full-Tree Cross-Document Links\n\nThe parent handoff table added by `140266be3e` names nonexistent `020/spec.md` and `021/spec.md` targets instead of the full nested-parent folder names (**P1 · NEW**). Canonical child docs also retain pre-migration repo paths: 012 uses stale snake_case sk-doc names, and 013 uses the removed `mcp_server` and `skill_advisor_hook.md` names (**P1 · PRE-EXISTING**). [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:133] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/012-sk-doc-routing-fixes/spec.md:112-125] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/013-skill-advisor-routing-fixes/tasks.md:67-74]\n\nThe nested 020 migration map's “New location” values duplicate `020-router-unification-program/` when interpreted relative to their own document and work only under an unstated packet-root base (**P2 · PRE-EXISTING**). Historical rename links were excluded, and no broken Markdown link-syntax target survived exact resolution. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/context-index.md:13-22]\n\n## Iteration 5 — Fleet Claims, Enforcement, and Lifecycle Completion\n\nThe parent’s new “7/7 hubs PASS” route-gold framing is broader than its canonical evidence: `sk-design` is counted as PASS with 0/0 applicable cases, while the verification report defines six applicable hubs. The false claim is the 7/7 coverage framing; 91/106 and 91/91 remain provenance-limited rather than disproven because raw run records are excluded. **P1 · NEW.** [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/implementation-summary.md:58-66] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n\nTwo nested lifecycle packets overclaim completion. `009-sk-doc-template-alignment` says Complete while its P0 strict-validation gate fails and only 12/13 P0 items are verified; `013-compiled-coverage-buildout` says Complete/100% while reporting 13/17 P1, 4/5 P2, and no formal operator sign-off. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/009-sk-doc-template-alignment/checklist.md:103-139] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:120-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:203-209]\n\nMandatory route proof confirmed generation/hash-bound compiled decisions for all seven hubs, but `parent-skill-check.cjs` still fails sk-design invariant 6a on unregistered `styles/`. Fleet activation is live; complete parent-hub invariant closure is not. **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**, reconfirmed. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs:29-42] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs:884-900] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/styles/README.md:1]\n\n## Iteration 6 — Nested Descendants Outside 020/007/015\n\nThe 021 parent lifecycle graph is stale: it remains planned and has no active-child pointer although phases 001-010 shipped and child 011 remains in progress. This is **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** and prevents deterministic descent to the active remediation packet. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/spec.md:10-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:45-48] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-documentation-quality-program/graph-metadata.json:105-106]\n\nTwo additional Level-2 descendants under 020 are structurally incomplete. `006-unified-refactor-research` claims complete/strict-clean but lacks plan, tasks, checklist, and implementation summary; `004-oob-glm-parallel-research` lacks the same files and also splits “Research complete” in spec from `in_progress` in graph. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**; `140266be3e` changed neither subtree. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:11-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:23-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:10-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40]\n\n## Iteration 7 — Eight Out-of-Box Idea Children\n\nAll eight `020/005` idea children declare Level 2 but lack the required planning and verification files; all eight strict validators exit 2. Children 001-004 additionally claim complete in spec and graph without checklist or implementation-summary evidence. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING** patterns. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:25] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/spec.md:69-71] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/001-compiled-policy-collapse/graph-metadata.json:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/008-trp-decomposition/spec.md:68-72]\n\nThe phase map overstates children 005-007 as complete while their child graphs remain in progress, and the local parent graph remains planned with a null active-child pointer despite seven completed rows and unfinished child 008. Both are **P1 · PRE-EXISTING**. The exact eight `children_ids` and all explicit canonical links resolve correctly; 008 truthfully remains unfinished. Commit `140266be3e` touched no path in this subtree, and object probes confirm all defects predate it. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/spec.md:37-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:6-15] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:41-44] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/005-oob-idea-deep-dives/graph-metadata.json:95-103]\n\n## Iteration 9 — Canonical Finding Reconciliation\n\nIterations 1–8 reconcile to **27 active findings: 22 P1 and 5 P2; 4 NEW and 23 PRE-EXISTING**. Exact duplicates were collapsed, the operator-gated/default-on claim was split into NEW `context-index.md` and PRE-EXISTING `spec.md` findings, and the combined 020/004 defect was split into a P1 required-file defect shared with 020/006 plus a P2 lifecycle-status disagreement. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:108-112] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:71-75] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/spec.md:10-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/006-unified-refactor-research/spec.md:23-31]\n\nThree severity changes were made explicit: broken parent handoff paths were downgraded P1→P2 because they are recoverable navigation references; nested 013 completion overclaim was downgraded P1→P2 because no P0 remains open and serving truth is supported; and 020/004's status-only portion was split/downgraded to P2 while its structural file-contract failure remains P1. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:124-134] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:120-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/004-oob-glm-parallel-research/graph-metadata.json:34-40]\n\nThe 91/106 and 91/91 figures are no longer a defect finding. Current canonical evidence supports that arithmetic over six applicable hubs; only the parent’s “7/7 hubs PASS” denominator remains **P1 · NEW**. Excluded raw run records limit provenance/reproduction but do not make the canonical figures false. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:152-161] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/020-router-unification-program/001-3-tier-consistency-standard/verification-report.md:47-55]\n\n## Iteration 10 — Terminal Mechanical Verification\n\nAll 27 canonical findings passed terminal source verification: 62/62 `file:line` anchors resolve to current non-empty ranges, and the totals remain **22 P1/5 P2** and **4 NEW/23 PRE-EXISTING**. No correction or duplicate defect finding was added. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-009.md:8-38]\n\nThe lineage now contains exactly iterations 001-010, deltas 001-010, and ten canonical state records inside the configured packet boundary. Earlier route strings were preserved append-only: iterations 6 and 8 append route-proof text to `resolved_route`, while iteration 10 carries the exact canonical `resolved_route`, explicit `route`, and structured no-subdispatch proof. No excluded artifact class was promoted as a defect. The configured tenth-iteration ceiling is reached with stop reason `maxIterationsReached`. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:3-18] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:2-11]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":61,"totalLines":61,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/research.md","time":{"start":1784866164670,"end":1784866164741}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0c940982c83315fd016a62e5748e7081918ebbcd3e1e8cffbb"}},"id":"prt_f92504fb8001wEy3nPMW3jmMg9","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f9250114b001CxPiUQfjwEPhw5"}}
