{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784866187421,"sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_eT2gUMVbIHEqAB7GCiUr4R4j","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","offset":1,"limit":150},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy\n2: \n3: ## 2. TOPIC\n4: Second-pass, expand-do-not-converge audit of the parent packet and its full 21-child tree, excluding frozen research, benchmark, lineage, output, log, and run-record artifacts.\n5: \n6: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n7: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n8: - [ ] Are all 21 direct child packets internally consistent and truthful about status and completion?\n9: - [ ] Do defects analogous to the known 012 and 017 failures exist in other direct children?\n10: - [ ] Do parent routing references match the live compiled-routing runtime and all seven hub routing surfaces?\n11: - [ ] Did commit 140266be3e introduce any new inconsistency, stale cross-reference, wrong metric, or broken link?\n12: - [ ] Are parent/child lifecycle metadata, children_ids, and derived.last_active_child_id truthful across nested topology?\n13: - [ ] Are links repo-rooted and valid, and are the 020/007 duplicate-012 collision and 015 sub-parent resume-safe?\n14: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n15: \n16: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n17: - Do not implement fixes.\n18: - Do not report frozen historical artifacts as defects.\n19: - Do not inspect `research/**`, `benchmark/**`, `lineages/**`, `*.out`, `*.log`, or run-record artifacts as defect candidates.\n20: - Do not write outside the bound lineage artifact directory.\n21: \n22: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n23: - Run exactly 10 iterations; convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.\n24: - Synthesize only after all 10 iterations are recorded and mechanically verified.\n25: \n26: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n27: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n28: - Direct-child consistency: four PRE-EXISTING P1 defects verified in 012, 015, 017, and 019.\n29: - Analogues beyond known defects: 015 and 019 have lifecycle/continuity contradictions; 013/014 and phase parents 020/021 were ruled out as false analogues.\n30: - Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n31: - Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n32: - Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n33: - Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n34: - Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n35: - Fleet claims: 7/7 route-gold framing is NEW and wrong in denominator scope; nested 009 and 013 overclaim completion; fleet activation is real but hard-invariant closure is incomplete.\n36: - Nested sampling: 021 parent metadata is stale; 020/004 and 020/006 are Level-2 packets missing required canonical files, with 004 also splitting lifecycle truth.\n37: - 020/005 subtree: all eight Level-2 children miss required files; completion and graph claims conflict; parent lifecycle/pointer metadata is stale.\n38: - Commit regression inventory: every canonical non-frozen hunk in `140266be3e` was reviewed; no additional finding survived deduplication.\n39: - Finding reconciliation: 27 canonical findings remain after merges, splits, downgrades, and provenance-limit exclusions.\n40: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n41: \n42: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n43: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n44: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n45: - Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n46: - Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n47: - Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n48: - Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n49: - Pairing claim inventory with live route proof, checker execution, and checklist arithmetic separated serving activation from closure and lifecycle truth (iteration 5).\n50: - Narrow branch inventories found Level-file and parent-pointer defects without repeating the primary 015 path (iteration 6).\n51: - Strict validation plus exact target and Git object probes efficiently classified all eight 020/005 children (iteration 7).\n52: - Zero-context changed-hunk review plus exact current-source checks closed the parent commit surface without inflating duplicate findings (iteration 8).\n53: - Stable canonical IDs exposed exact duplicates, mixed provenance, severity downgrades, and structural/lifecycle splits (iteration 9).\n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n55: \n56: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n57: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n58: - Broad recursive validator output mixed nested descendants into direct-child evidence; use narrow direct-file verification for subsequent topology passes (iteration 1).\n59: - Exact 91/106 and 91/91 reproduction is unavailable from promoted non-frozen evidence; treat these as provenance gaps rather than false values (iteration 3).\n60: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n61: \n62: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n63: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n64: - Full direct-child inventory is complete; do not repeat unless canonical files change.\n65: - The 020/005 eight-child inventory is complete; do not repeat unless canonical files change.\n66: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n67: \n68: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n69: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n70: - Treating planned 013/014 implementation-summary absence as analogous to 012.\n71: - Treating lean phase-parent 020/021 heavy-doc absence as a required-file defect.\n72: - Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n73: - Treating the 015 child-count claim as wrong; the count is 14, while its phase map exposes only 12.\n74: - Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n75: - Treating generic backticked filenames or logical `children_ids` as broken filesystem links without contextual/schema resolution.\n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n77: \n78: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n79: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n80: - Terminal mechanical verification and synthesis remain pending.\n81: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n82: \n83: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n84: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n85: Mechanically verify all 27 canonical finding anchors and counts, validate all 10 lineage artifacts and route fields, and record terminal max-iterations evidence for synthesis.\n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n87: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n88: \n89: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n90: - The first audit covered parent-level docs only and commit `140266be3e` applied its findings.\n91: - Known child defects to verify: `012-sk-doc-routing-fixes` required-file/LEVEL_MATCH inconsistency and `017-system-code-graph-routing-research` `_memory` frontmatter violation.\n92: - The code graph is empty, so direct file evidence is authoritative for this run.\n93: - No packet root `resource-map.md` exists.\n94: \n95: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n96: - Max iterations: 10\n97: - Stop policy: max-iterations\n98: - Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol`\n99: - Every finding must include real `file:line` evidence, P1/P2 severity, and NEW/PRE-EXISTING classification.\n\n(End of file - total 99 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nSecond-pass, expand-do-not-converge audit of the parent packet and its full 21-child tree, excluding frozen research, benchmark, lineage, output, log, and run-record artifacts.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Are all 21 direct child packets internally consistent and truthful about status and completion?\n- [ ] Do defects analogous to the known 012 and 017 failures exist in other direct children?\n- [ ] Do parent routing references match the live compiled-routing runtime and all seven hub routing surfaces?\n- [ ] Did commit 140266be3e introduce any new inconsistency, stale cross-reference, wrong metric, or broken link?\n- [ ] Are parent/child lifecycle metadata, children_ids, and derived.last_active_child_id truthful across nested topology?\n- [ ] Are links repo-rooted and valid, and are the 020/007 duplicate-012 collision and 015 sub-parent resume-safe?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Do not implement fixes.\n- Do not report frozen historical artifacts as defects.\n- Do not inspect `research/**`, `benchmark/**`, `lineages/**`, `*.out`, `*.log`, or run-record artifacts as defect candidates.\n- Do not write outside the bound lineage artifact directory.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nSecond-pass, expand-do-not-converge audit of the parent packet and its full 21-child tree, excluding frozen research, benchmark, lineage, output, log, and run-record artifacts.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Are all 21 direct child packets internally consistent and truthful about status and completion?\n- [ ] Do defects analogous to the known 012 and 017 failures exist in other direct children?\n- [ ] Do parent routing references match the live compiled-routing runtime and all seven hub routing surfaces?\n- [ ] Did commit 140266be3e introduce any new inconsistency, stale cross-reference, wrong metric, or broken link?\n- [ ] Are parent/child lifecycle metadata, children_ids, and derived.last_active_child_id truthful across nested topology?\n- [ ] Are links repo-rooted and valid, and are the 020/007 duplicate-012 collision and 015 sub-parent resume-safe?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Do not implement fixes.\n- Do not report frozen historical artifacts as defects.\n- Do not inspect `research/**`, `benchmark/**`, `lineages/**`, `*.out`, `*.log`, or run-record artifacts as defect candidates.\n- Do not write outside the bound lineage artifact directory.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Run exactly 10 iterations; convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.\n- Synthesize only after all 10 iterations are recorded and mechanically verified.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- Direct-child consistency: four PRE-EXISTING P1 defects verified in 012, 015, 017, and 019.\n- Analogues beyond known defects: 015 and 019 have lifecycle/continuity contradictions; 013/014 and phase parents 020/021 were ruled out as false analogues.\n- Commit impact at direct-child depth: `140266be3e` changed no canonical direct-child packet file, so none of these defects is NEW.\n- Nested resume topology: null pointers at 020 and 020/007 block deterministic descent; 020/007/015 has a stale phase map and stale pointer.\n- Duplicate phase prefix: full canonical IDs disambiguate the two `012-*` siblings, but numeric-only selection is ambiguous.\n- Parent/runtime conformance: live routing is compiled-authoritative and default-on for all seven hubs; parent canon contains new and pre-existing contradictions.\n- Canonical link audit: one NEW parent handoff break and three PRE-EXISTING stale/ambiguous path contracts were verified.\n- Fleet claims: 7/7 route-gold framing is NEW and wrong in denominator scope; nested 009 and 013 overclaim completion; fleet activation is real but hard-invariant closure is incomplete.\n- Nested sampling: 021 parent metadata is stale; 020/004 and 020/006 are Level-2 packets missing required canonical files, with 004 also splitting lifecycle truth.\n- 020/005 subtree: all eight Level-2 children miss required files; completion and graph claims conflict; parent lifecycle/pointer metadata is stale.\n- Commit regression inventory: every canonical non-frozen hunk in `140266be3e` was reviewed; no additional finding survived deduplication.\n- Finding reconciliation: 27 canonical findings remain after merges, splits, downgrades, and provenance-limit exclusions.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- Direct-depth inventory plus narrow strict validation separated genuine defects from planned-packet and phase-parent false positives (iteration 1).\n- Narrow metadata, phase-map, and live-resolver reads established actual resume behavior without relying on frozen artifacts (iteration 2).\n- Seven-hub inventory, live resolver calls, checker execution, and commit attribution separated authored, benchmark, and serving authority (iteration 3).\n- Separating Markdown links, explicit repo paths, contextual backticks, and schema-owned logical IDs avoided broad-scan false positives (iteration 4).\n- Pairing claim inventory with live route proof, checker execution, and checklist arithmetic separated serving activation from closure and lifecycle truth (iteration 5).\n- Narrow branch inventories found Level-file and parent-pointer defects without repeating the primary 015 path (iteration 6).\n- Strict validation plus exact target and Git object probes efficiently classified all eight 020/005 children (iteration 7).\n- Zero-context changed-hunk review plus exact current-source checks closed the parent commit surface without inflating duplicate findings (iteration 8).\n- Stable canonical IDs exposed exact duplicates, mixed provenance, severity downgrades, and structural/lifecycle splits (iteration 9).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n- Broad recursive validator output mixed nested descendants into direct-child evidence; use narrow direct-file verification for subsequent topology passes (iteration 1).\n- Exact 91/106 and 91/91 reproduction is unavailable from promoted non-frozen evidence; treat these as provenance gaps rather than false values (iteration 3).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n- Full direct-child inventory is complete; do not repeat unless canonical files change.\n- The 020/005 eight-child inventory is complete; do not repeat unless canonical files change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n- Treating planned 013/014 implementation-summary absence as analogous to 012.\n- Treating lean phase-parent 020/021 heavy-doc absence as a required-file defect.\n- Classifying direct-child defects as NEW from `140266be3e`.\n- Treating the 015 child-count claim as wrong; the count is 14, while its phase map exposes only 12.\n- Treating complete canonical `last_active_child_id` values as ambiguous across duplicate numeric prefixes.\n- Treating generic backticked filenames or logical `children_ids` as broken filesystem links without contextual/schema resolution.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n- Terminal mechanical verification and synthesis remain pending.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nMechanically verify all 27 canonical finding anchors and counts, validate all 10 lineage artifacts and route fields, and record terminal max-iterations evidence for synthesis.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n- The first audit covered parent-level docs only and commit `140266be3e` applied its findings.\n- Known child defects to verify: `012-sk-doc-routing-fixes` required-file/LEVEL_MATCH inconsistency and `017-system-code-graph-routing-research` `_memory` frontmatter violation.\n- The code graph is empty, so direct file evidence is authoritative for this run.\n- No packet root `resource-map.md` exists.\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 10\n- Stop policy: max-iterations\n- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol`\n- Every finding must include real `file:line` evidence, P1/P2 severity, and NEW/PRE-EXISTING classification.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":99,"totalLines":99,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1784866187413,"end":1784866187420}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04c20fbbe78a785d016a62e58b4bd88191945478c2abb4c0bb"}},"id":"prt_f9250a893001SKLGuj540UodcP","sessionID":"ses_06df05187ffeYScgmqkSqD6Jbx","messageID":"msg_f925058e80018DJ3YalcYA1Hzn"}}
