 wrong metric, or broken link?\n-- [ ] Are parent/child lifecycle metadata, children_ids, and derived.last_active_child_id truthful across nested topology?\n-- [ ] Are links repo-rooted and valid, and are the 020/007 duplicate-012 collision and 015 sub-parent resume-safe?\n+- [x] Are all 21 direct child packets internally consistent and truthful about status and completion?\n+- [x] Do defects analogous to the known 012 and 017 failures exist in other direct children?\n+- [x] Do parent routing references match the live compiled-routing runtime and all seven hub routing surfaces?\n+- [x] Did commit 140266be3e introduce any new inconsistency, stale cross-reference, wrong metric, or broken link?\n+- [x] Are parent/child lifecycle metadata, children_ids, and derived.last_active_child_id truthful across nested topology?\n+- [x] Are links repo-rooted and valid, and are the 020/007 duplicate-012 collision and 015 sub-parent resume-safe?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n \n ## 4. NON-GOALS\n - Do not implement fixes.\n@@ -76,14 +76,14 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n-- Terminal mechanical verification and synthesis remain pending.\n+None. Remediation ownership is outside this research-only lineage.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Mechanically verify all 27 canonical finding anchors and counts, validate all 10 lineage artifacts and route fields, and record terminal max-iterations evidence for synthesis.\n+Research complete. Use `research.md` as the canonical synthesis for remediation planning.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n","additions":8,"deletions":8},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/round-3-sol/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl","rela